          "path": "_m/g/c/m/z/museum-of-liverpool-wp/liverpool-window-view-museum-o.jpg",
          "filename": "Liverpool window view - Museum of Liverpool (10628911285).jpg",
          "caption": "View from the window at the International Slavery Museum, Albert Dock, Liverpool.\nThe Liverpool Waterfront. It has changed so much since the days of the transatlantic slave trade ended.\nThe three famous 20th century Pier Head buildings stand on the site of George's Dock where slave ships bound for Africa loaded their goods.\nThe two dry docks, in front of the Great Western Railway building, were built in the 18th century, Slave ships were repaired in these docks. They are a vivid reminder of the horrors of Liverpool's slave trading, and monuments to the commercial success of 18th century Liverpool.\nMuseum of Liverpool.\nIn front is the Pilotage Building.\n\nTo the right is the Great Western Railway building.",
          "alt": "View from the window at the International Slavery Museum, Albert Dock, Liverpool.\nThe Liverpool Waterfront. It has changed so much since the days of the transatlantic slave trade ended.\nThe three famous 20th century Pier Head buildings stand on the site of George's Dock where slave ships bound for Africa loaded their goods.\nThe two dry docks, in front of the Great Western Railway building, were built in the 18th century, Slave ships were repaired in these docks. They are a vivid reminder of the horrors of Liverpool's slave trading, and monuments to the commercial success of 18th century Liverpool.\nMuseum of Liverpool.\nIn front is the Pilotage Building.\n\nTo the right is the Great Western Railway building.",
          "width": 4288,
          "height": 3216,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Elliott Brown from Birmingham, United Kingdom",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liverpool_window_view_-_Museum_of_Liverpool_(10628911285).jpg",
